    "Model exhibits a strong upward bias when recent history shows a sustained uptrend (e.g., Example 1), consistently overestimating the 30-day average by 4-6 EUR.",
    "When sentiment turns negative (-0.25) immediately following a price spike, the model fails to capture the subsequent mean reversion and volatility contraction, resulting in significant underestimation of downside risk.",
    "The model displays severe lag in reacting to sudden price drops (e.g., Example 4), maintaining an upward trajectory despite clear downward momentum in the true outcome.",
    "Forecasts are overly smooth and lack the high-frequency volatility observed in actual EU ETS outcomes, leading to systematic underestimation of range expansion.",
    "When sentiment history shows mixed signals (positive/negative) within a short window, the model defaults to a conservative mean rather than adapting to the immediate trend reversal."
